 "readme": "# Network Anomaly Detection System (FYP)\n\nThis repository contains the Final Year Project (FYP) source code for an Adaptive Threat Detection & Mitigation (ATDM) Network Anomaly Detection System. The system is designed to simulate network traffic, extract features in real-time, detect anomalies using Graph Neural Networks (GNN) and machine learning models (XGBoost), and perform automated mitigation on SDN topologies.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThe system consists of three main components:\n\n1. **Backend (Inference Engine & GNN Models)**: A FastAPI-based server that hosts the machine learning models. It receives traffic data, performs real-time inference, and detects anomalies using custom GNN scalers (StandardScaler, RobustScaler, TriChannelScaler).\n2. **Frontend & Topology Controller**: A SDN controller (Ryu-based / Simple Switch 13 and ATDM) and web dashboard that manages the network topology (using Open vSwitch and Linux namespaces), simulates attack scenarios, and extracts flow features.\n3. **Benchmark & Evaluation Pipeline**: Automated evaluation framework for running 6 attack scenarios (Probe, DoS, DDoS, SQLi, Credential Attack, Exfiltration) across Small and Large network topologies, generating paper figures (Figures 1–6) and exporting full experimental results to Excel.\n\n## Repository Structure\n\n```text\nfyp/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── app.py                      # FastAPI inference server\n│   ├── benchmark/\n│   │   ├── benchmark.py            # Primary benchmark execution engine\n│   │   ├── generate_all_figures.py # Master figure & Excel workbook generator\n│   │   ├── controllers/            # SDN controllers (Simple Switch 13, ATDM)\n│   │   ├── config/scenarios/       # Scenario definitions (probe, dos, ddos, etc.)\n│   │   └── results/final_atdm_runs/# Verified 24-run benchmark JSON dataset\n│   ├── gnn_compare/\n│   │   ├── fig1_rescale_retrain.py # GNN feature scaling benchmark (Standard vs Robust vs Tri-Channel)\n│   │   └── fig1_rescale_vs_retrain.png # Figure 1 output\n│   ├── scalers/                    # Pre-fitted feature scalers (.pkl)\n│   └── models/                     # Trained PyTorch GNN model checkpoints\n├── final_experiment_results.xlsx   # Complete 9-sheet Excel workbook\n├── README.md                       # Project documentation\n└── .gitignore                      # Git ignore rules\n```\n\n## Quick Start & Reproducing Benchmarks\n\n### 1. Environment Setup\n```bash\npython3 -m venv fypenv\nsource fypenv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements.txt  # Or install pytorch, torch-geometric, matplotlib, openpyxl, pandas, scikit-learn\n```\n\n### 2. Run GNN Feature Scaling Experiment (Figure 1)\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=backend python3 backend/gnn_compare/fig1_rescale_retrain.py\n```\n- Outputs: `backend/gnn_compare/fig1_rescale_vs_retrain.png` and `backend/gnn_compare/fig1_f1_raw.csv`.\n\n### 3. Generate All Paper Figures (Figures 2–6) and Excel Workbook\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=backend python3 backend/benchmark/generate_all_figures.py\n```\n- Figures generated in `backend/benchmark/figures/`:\n  - `fig2_latency_timeline.png` (User-perceived latency across 6.5-minute timeline)\n  - `fig3_security_preservation.png` (Web Server & Database protection scores)\n  - `fig4_service_availability.png` (Service Continuity Scores across scenarios)\n  - `fig5_bandwidth_util.png` (Bandwidth utilization percentage timeline)\n  - `fig6_throughput_timeline.png` (Benign user throughput timeline)\n- Excel Workbook: `final_experiment_results.xlsx` (9 formatted sheets with raw data and aggregated statistics).\n\n## System Requirements\n\n- **Operating System**: Linux (Ubuntu 20.04+ recommended; relies on OVS and Linux network namespaces)\n- **Python**: Python 3.10+ (tested on Python 3.12)\n- **Privileges**: Root/sudo access required for SDN topology simulation and network interface management\n- **Hardware**: GPU recommended for training GNN models\n",
